# M4.29.2 staged payload chatops traversal failure

Date: 2026-08-28

## Symptom

All eight staged artifact hashes matched commit
`d0838f7367940e00192e6599d6129bc11758e520`, all shell syntax checks passed and
all three staged units passed `systemd-analyze verify`. The additional
pre-install `--check` under the future runtime identity `chatops` failed before
execution with `Permission denied`.

## Cause

The root-private staging directory and staged scripts were mode `0700`, so
`chatops` could not traverse or execute them. This is a staging permission
issue, not a script or Control failure.

## Impact

- installed artifacts changed: no;
- daemon reload performed: no;
- service restarted: no;
- Control changed: no;
- Adult Candidate changed: no;
- affected services remain safely stopped.

## Resolution

Keep the recovery archive itself root-only. Change only the staged payload
directory and staged scripts to `root:chatops` with group-read/traverse modes,
repeat every staged hash and the `chatops --check`, then install only if all
checks succeed.

The first permission adjustment of the payload itself was insufficient because
the parent recovery directory correctly remained root-only. No parent recovery
permission is relaxed. Root instead opens the already hashed staged script and
passes its bytes over standard input to a Bash process running as `chatops`.
This validates the exact payload under the runtime identity without granting
access to the recovery tree.
